# ===================================================================
# UNIVERSAL MEDIA STUDIO - BACKEND ENVIRONMENT EXAMPLE
# Copy to .env or paste in Coolify Backend Application Environment Variables
# ===================================================================

# Server Port
PORT=5000

# Whitelist your deployed frontend domains here (comma-separated):
FRONTEND_URL=https://humantalking.com,http://localhost:3000

# Node Environment
NODE_ENV=production

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUTUBE BOT-GUARD BYPASS CONFIGURATION
# -------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Proof-of-Origin (PO) Token Provider Container URL
# (Set automatically by docker-compose, defaults to internal sidecar):
POT_PROVIDER_URL=http://pot-provider:4416

# 2. YouTube Authentication Cookies (RECOMMENDED for Datacenter VPS)
# When deployed on a Cloud VPS (Hetzner, OVH, DigitalOcean, etc.), YouTube flags
# the server's datacenter IP and requires "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot".
# How to get:
#   a) Log into a throwaway/burner Google account in Chrome/Firefox.
#   b) Install the Chrome extension "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY".
#   c) Open youtube.com, export cookies in Netscape format.
#   d) Copy the entire text content and paste it as the value of YOUTUBE_COOKIES.
# YOUTUBE_COOKIES="# Netscape HTTP Cookie File\n# ..."

# 3. Outbound Proxy (Alternative to Cookies)
# If you don't want to use cookies, route yt-dlp traffic through a residential
# proxy or socks5 tunnel so YouTube does not see a datacenter IP:
# Example: YTDLP_PROXY=http://user:password@proxy.example.com:8080
# Example: YTDLP_PROXY=socks5://127.0.0.1:1080
# YTDLP_PROXY=
